==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*unþijō}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*unt-}}. Germanic cognates include Old Saxon [[uðia|ūðia]], Old High German [[undea]], Old Norse [[unnr]], [[uðr]]. The Indo-European root is also the source of Latin [[unda]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/yːθ/|lang=ang}}

